## 2.0.0-beta19

### Swiper Block — Hash Navigation Link Active States

Enhanced hash navigation tracking to properly synchronize hash-based navigation links with swiper slide state.

- **Hash tracking registry** — when hash navigation is enabled, each Swiper instance now registers itself in a global `window.methodSwipers` object on initialization, allowing cross-swiper hash state monitoring.
- **Active hash link styling** — new global tracking script monitors hash navigation across all swipers and applies the `.method-hash-active` class to any link whose `href` matches the currently active slide's hash (via `data-hash` attribute). The active state is updated on slide change, page load, and browser back/forward navigation.
- **Listener attachment** — the tracking system safely attaches event listeners to swipers as they initialize, using a `Set` to prevent duplicate listeners and a retry interval to handle asynchronous registration. The listener setup occurs only once per page (`methodHashTrackingLoaded` flag).
- Removed unused `enqueue_method_swiper_assets()` function and associated commented-out code.



## 2.0.0-beta18

### Theme Icons — Shared Icon System

Custom icons are now a theme-level concept rather than a Theme Button feature, so a single icon set can be reused by any block that offers an icon picker.

- New `method_get_theme_icons()` (`lib/blocks.php`) assembles the set from the new `method_theme_icons` filter; icons added through the existing `method_block_theme_button_icons` filter are merged in, so child themes already supplying button icons work unchanged.
- The icon set is localized into the block editor globally as `methodGlobalData.icons` (the Theme Button–specific `buttonIcons` localization has been removed).
- New `method_register_theme_icons()` also registers the set with WordPress' icon library (`wp_register_icon_collection()` / `wp_register_icon()`, when available) under a **Method** collection, so theme icons appear in core's icon pickers. Set `'omit' => true` on an icon to keep it out of the WordPress collection while leaving it available to Method's own controls.
- **Theme Button** now reads icons from the shared set on both sides — the editor dropdowns from `methodGlobalData.icons`, the render callback via `method_get_theme_icons()` — and the Before/After Icon dropdowns gain an explicit **None** option.

### Method Swiper — Arrow Icons, Navigation Colors & Outside Pagination

- **Custom arrow icons** — when "Show arrows" is enabled, new **Previous Arrow** and **Next Arrow** dropdowns (new `prevIcon` / `nextIcon` attributes) swap the default chevrons for any theme icon. Arrow icons are now wrapped in `.method-swiper-icon` spans and the buttons are flex-centered within their 44×44px targets, in both the editor preview and the frontend markup.
- **Navigation colors** — new **Navigation Arrows** (`textColor`) and **Pagination** (`linkColor`) color controls via `MethodColorControls`. CSS is generated per breakpoint on both sides: `MethodStyleTag` in the editor, `method_get_block_responsive_styles()` plus the CSS collector on the frontend.
- **Outside pagination** — a new **Place pagination outside** toggle (`altPagination` attribute) renders the pagination bullets outside the Swiper container, alongside the navigation arrows, instead of overlaying the slides. Applies to both the editor preview and the frontend.
- **Restyled bullets** — pagination bullets are now outlined (transparent fill with a 2px `currentColor` border) with the active bullet filled, so they follow the new Pagination color.
- **Loop disabled** — the frontend Swiper config now sets `loop: false` (previously `true`), matching the editor preview and avoiding the duplicate-slide quirks loop mode caused with hash navigation.

### Method Swiper — Theme Breakpoints & Canvas-Aware Editor Preview

- The mobile/tablet/desktop tiers for "Slides per view" and "Space between" now follow the theme's configured breakpoints instead of hardcoded 768px/1024px values. On the frontend, new `method_swiper_get_breakpoints()` derives the tablet and desktop min-widths from `method_get_block_breakpoints()` (`tablet_min` and `tablet_max` + 1).
- New editor hooks — `useCanvasWindow()` and `useCanvasViewport()` (`lib/blocks/hooks/useCanvasViewport.js`) — resolve which Method breakpoint tier the editor canvas is currently in by running media queries against the canvas iframe's own window, using the same localized breakpoints (`methodGlobalData.breakpoints`).
- The editor Swiper preview is now initialised with the resolved tier's per-view/spacing values rather than Swiper's own `breakpoints` option, which evaluated `matchMedia` against the top admin window and therefore never tracked the device preview or a resized canvas. The preview re-initialises when the canvas crosses a breakpoint, keeping it in sync with the frontend.

### Core Extensions — Full Typography Set

- The responsive controls for `core/paragraph`, `core/heading`, and `core/list` now include the typography options introduced in beta17 — **Font Family**, **Font Appearance** (style + weight), **Letter Case**, and **Letter Spacing** — alongside the existing size, line-height, and alignment controls, wired through the editor controls, the editor CSS map, and the frontend CSS config.
- Editor CSS for core-extension overrides is now emitted with `!important`, via a new `isImportant` prop on `MethodStyleTag`, so responsive overrides reliably beat core/theme.json specificity inside the editor canvas. Frontend output is unchanged.
- Breakpoint defaults have been slimmed down (JS `RESPONSIVE_DEFAULTS` and PHP `method_core_extensions_get_defaults()`): the mobile, tablet, and wide breakpoints now default to just `enabled: false` rather than a full set of zeroed padding/margin/typography values, so untouched breakpoints no longer carry default values.

## 2.0.0-beta17

### New Block — Marquee (`method/looping-alert`)

A horizontally scrolling text ticker. A single line of **Alert Text** is repeated with a **Separator** between each copy and scrolls continuously across the block's width. Referred to as "Looping Alert" during development, so the block directory (`method-looping-alert`) and block name retain that name; the inserter title is **Method Marquee**. (Closes #10)

- **Alert Options** panel — Alert Text, Separator, and a **Scroll Speed** range (0–100). Speed is converted to a constant pixels-per-second rate (3px/s per unit, so the default of 25 ≈ 75px/s) rather than a fixed animation duration, so the scroll speed stays consistent regardless of text length or container width. Speed 0 pauses the marquee.
- **Optional link** — the block toolbar's link control wraps the entire marquee in an `<a>` (with "open in new tab" support). When a link is set, a **Background Shade** color control is also exposed alongside the text and background colors.
- **Styling** — top/bottom padding and margin, border and border radius, and the full new typography set (font family, appearance, size, letter case, letter spacing), all per breakpoint via the responsive tabs. Supports wide and full alignment.
- **Frontend** (`src/frontend.js`, registered as the block's `viewScript`) — the PHP render outputs a single text + separator unit; the script measures it, clones it enough times to fill the container (plus one), then duplicates the whole group (`aria-hidden`) so the CSS `translateX(-50%)` animation loops seamlessly. Layout is recalculated on container resize (`ResizeObserver`) and after web fonts finish loading. The animation is disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
- **Editor preview** (`src/LoopingAlertMarquee.js`) mirrors the frontend markup and animation, sharing the same measurement/timing math (`src/marquee.js`) so both behave identically.
- Registered in `lib/blocks.php`; global styles for `.method-looping-alert` added to `global.scss`.

### Typography Controls — Font Family, Appearance, Letter Case & Letter Spacing

- **`MethodTypographyControls`** gains an `include` prop, following the opt-in pattern used by the other Method control components. The default (`['fontSize', 'lineHeight', 'textAlign']`) matches previous behaviour, so existing blocks are unchanged. New options:
  - `fontFamily` — a **Font Family** picker populated from `theme.json` font families (custom, theme, and default origins merged, as core's typography panel does).
  - `fontAppearance` — a combined **Font Appearance** (style + weight) control, stored as separate `fontStyle` and `fontWeight` responsive settings.
  - `textTransform` — **Letter Case**.
  - `letterSpacing` — **Letter Spacing**.
  - "Reset all" now clears every typography setting, including the new ones.
- CSS generation handles the new properties on both sides: `MethodStyleTag.jsx` (editor) and `method_get_block_css_declarations()` in `lib/blocks.php` (frontend) now emit `font-family`, `font-style`, `font-weight`, `text-transform`, and `letter-spacing` from responsive settings. `textColor` is also accepted as an alias for the `color` CSS-map key.

### Block Naming & Inspector UI

- **All top-level Method blocks are now prefixed with "Method" in the inserter** (e.g. *Method Section*, *Method Container*, *Method Swiper*) to avoid confusion with similarly named core blocks (#6). Block *names* (`method/section`, etc.) are unchanged, so existing content is unaffected. Renamed: Accordion, Advanced Grid, Basic Grid, Breadcrumb, Buttons, Container, Fitted Image, Flex Container, Fluid Video, Marquee, Scrollspy, Section, Site Navbar, Social Nav, Swiper, Swiper Gallery, and Tabs. (Closes #6)
- **`MethodResponsiveTabs`** — the "Responsive Behavior" panel is no longer a collapsible (and collapsed-by-default) `PanelBody`; it now renders as an always-visible section with a heading so the breakpoint tabs are immediately accessible.

### Visibility Toggle — Flex Item & Advanced Grid Column

- The `hide` option introduced in beta15 is now wired up for the **Flex Item** (`method/flex-item`) and **Advanced Grid Column** (`method/advanced-grid-col`) blocks across the mobile, tablet, and wide breakpoints, in both the editor (`MethodAddtControls` with `include={['hide']}`) and the frontend render callbacks.

### Responsive Embeds (opt-in)

- New `method_responsive_embed_wrap()` in `lib/theme-setup.php` wraps oEmbed output (`embed_oembed_html` and `oembed_result` filters) whose `<iframe>` declares a `width` and `height` in a `.method-embed` container with an `--embed-ratio` custom property derived from those dimensions. Companion styles set `aspect-ratio: var(--embed-ratio, 16 / 9)` on the wrapper and stretch the iframe to fill it. Already-wrapped output is skipped.
- Opt in from a child theme with `add_theme_support( 'method-responsive-embeds' );`.

### Responsive Editing Flag (groundwork)

- New `method_configure_responsive_editing()` adds a `responsiveEditingEnabled` setting to the block editor (`block_editor_settings_all`). It defaults to `false`; child themes can enable it with `add_theme_support( 'method-responsive-editing' );` or the `method/responsive_editing_enabled` filter. This only affects the editing UI — rendering of saved responsive styles is unaffected. Note that no editor component reads this flag yet; it is exposed in this release so the responsive tabs can be gated by it in a future update. (Closes #2)

### CSS Collector

- **`Method_CSS_Collector`** (`lib/class-method-css-collector.php`) now flushes twice: at `wp_head` (priority 100) as before, and again at `wp_footer` (priority 20). Previously any CSS registered after the head had been output — blocks rendered during the template, such as nav panels, hooked content, or late-rendered blocks — was silently discarded. Late additions are now printed in a second `<style id="block-instance-styles-1">` tag. Dedupe by `block_id` applies across both pending and already-flushed styles.
- New cache-integration primitives: `snapshot()` returns the keys collected so far, `diff_since( $snapshot )` returns everything added since, and `inject( $entries )` re-adds previously captured CSS (with dedupe). These allow fragment-caching layers to store a block's CSS beside its cached markup and restore it on a cache hit.
- The production minifier no longer strips whitespace around `+`, which was corrupting `calc()` expressions (e.g. `calc(100% + 1rem)` → the invalid `calc(100%+1rem)`).

### Build Tooling — Single `package.json` (Closes #11)

- All per-block `package.json` files have been removed in favour of a single `lib/blocks/package.json`, so `@wordpress/scripts` only needs to be installed once (`npm install` inside `lib/blocks`).
- New `lib/blocks/build-all.js` (`npm run build`) builds every block directory that contains a `src/` folder, running `wp-scripts build` with `--webpack-src-dir` / `--output-path` pointed at each block. Pass a name or prefix to build a subset (e.g. `npm run build method-section`). `build:block` and `start:block` scripts expose `wp-scripts build` / `wp-scripts start` for single-block use.
- All blocks were recompiled with the shared toolchain; a stray `method-accordion/src.zip` was removed from the repo.

### Fixes

- **Container & Section — theme button link color** — the `linkColor` selector is now `a:not(.method-theme-button)` (frontend render for both blocks, and the Section editor preview), so theme buttons placed inside a Container or Section keep their own button colors instead of inheriting the block's link color.
- **Container** — the tablet and wide **Align Items** controls were bound to the `mobile` breakpoint, so changes on those tabs wrote to (and displayed) the mobile value. Each tab now targets its own breakpoint.
- **Container & Section** — the `useParallax` (and Section's `unconstrained`) attributes declared the invalid type `bool` in `block.json`; corrected to `boolean`.
- **Section — editor spacing** — `.method-section` now explicitly zeroes `margin-block-start`/`margin-block-end`, and `theme.json` sets `method/section` top/bottom margin to `0`, removing the unwanted gap that appeared between consecutive sections in the editor.
- **Fitted Image** — `borderRadius` and `boxShadow` are now also applied to the `.method-block-shade` overlay (editor and frontend), so the shade follows the block's rounded corners rather than squaring them off.
- **Advanced Grid — column content margins** — the first-child reset now uses `margin-block-start: 0` (so it also applies to blocks that set logical margins), and the last-child bottom-margin reset has been removed so trailing blocks retain their own bottom spacing.
- **Swiper — hash navigation** — now uses `replaceState: true`, so moving between slides no longer adds a browser history entry per slide.
- **Swiper — scroll to slide start** — the `slideChange` handler now tracks `realIndex` and bails when it hasn't changed, preventing spurious scrolls when Swiper's `loop` mode swaps between a slide and its duplicate. The scroll also uses `behavior: 'instant'` rather than `smooth`, so the slider is repositioned immediately on navigation.
- **Theme Options — Diagnostic Details** now includes the server's PHP version.

## 2.0.0-beta16

### Swiper Block — Fade Effect, Hash Navigation & Scroll-to-Slide

Three additions to the **Swiper** block (`method/swiper` + `method/swiper-slide`), all configured from the inspector and reflected in both the editor and on the frontend.

- **Fade (crossfade) effect** — a new **Effect** panel adds a **Fade (crossfade)** toggle. When enabled, the frontend uses Swiper's `fade` effect with `crossFade: true`, showing a single slide at a time; the "Slides per view" and "Space between" panels are hidden, since they no longer apply. The editor preview also drops to one slide at a time, but deliberately keeps the normal (non-stacked) slide layout rather than the real fade: Swiper's fade effect overlaps every slide in the same position, and the top-most (last) slide would then swallow clicks meant for the others, making it impossible to reliably click a slide to edit it. The crossfade transition itself is therefore applied on the frontend only.
- **Hash navigation** — a new **Hash navigation** toggle on the parent block enables Swiper's `hashNavigation` (`watchState: true`), keeping the URL hash in sync with the active slide and jumping to the matching slide on load and on browser back/forward. Each **Swiper Slide** child block gains a **Slide hash** field (new `hash` attribute) that is output as a `data-hash` attribute on the slide in both the editor and on the frontend.
- **Scroll to slide start** — a new **Scroll to slide start** toggle that appears only when hash navigation is enabled. On the frontend, navigating to a new slide smoothly scrolls the page to the top of the slider — useful when slides vary substantially in height. The handler is bound after Swiper initialises, so the initial hash jump on page load does not trigger a scroll; only genuine navigation (arrows, pagination, or a hash change) does. The option is also gated server-side so it has no effect unless hash navigation is on.

### Fixes

- **Google Analytics** — `method_inject_gtag()` (`lib/theme-setup.php`) now builds the `gtag.js` loader URL from the configured **Tag ID** (`ga_id`) theme option instead of a hardcoded tracking ID, so the loader script and the inline config reference the same property.

## 2.0.0-beta15

### New Block — Swiper (`method/swiper` + `method/swiper-slide`)

A responsive content carousel built on [Swiper](https://swiperjs.com). The parent **Swiper** block holds one or more **Swiper Slide** child blocks, each of which is a full inner-blocks container that can hold any other Method or core blocks.

- **Responsive slides-per-view and spacing** — separate Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile controls for both "Slides per view" (1–6) and "Space between" (0–120px). Values are mobile-first: the mobile setting is the base, with tablet (≥768px) and desktop (≥1024px) applied as Swiper breakpoint overrides. The same breakpoints are used in the editor preview and on the frontend.
- **Navigation toggles** — "Show arrows" and "Show pagination" toggles in the inspector. Prev/next arrows use inline Bootstrap chevron SVGs with visually-hidden labels; pagination renders clickable bullets.
- **Editor parity** — the block initialises a live Swiper instance inside the editor that mirrors the frontend config. Touch/drag is disabled and click handling is left to Gutenberg so slides remain selectable and editable; Swiper observers keep the instance in sync as slides are added, removed, or their contents change.
- **Custom slide appender** — an "Add slide" button is rendered outside the Swiper track (so it isn't sized or clipped like a slide) and inserts a new `method/swiper-slide` without stealing focus.
- The frontend render callback outputs a per-instance Swiper config with a unique ID, `loop: true`, and `autoHeight: true`. Navigation/pagination markup and config are only emitted when the corresponding toggle is enabled.
- New global styles for `.method-swiper` lay out the prev/arrow/track/next row via flexbox with 44×44px arrow targets.
- `lib/blocks.php` registers the new block.

### Additional Options — Visibility Toggle

- **`MethodAddtControls`** gains a new `hide` option, opt-in via the `include` array (now `['overflow', 'zIndex', 'hide']` by default). The "Visibility" tools-panel item exposes a **Hide** toggle that hides the block for the selected breakpoint by setting `display: none` and `visibility: hidden`.
- CSS generation handles `hide` on both sides: `method_get_block_css_declarations()` (`lib/blocks.php`) emits the declarations on the frontend, and `MethodStyleTag.jsx` emits them in the editor preview.
- The Basic Grid **Item** block (`method-basic-grid`) now wires up the visibility toggle across the mobile, tablet, and wide breakpoints, mapped to the item's outer wrapper selector.

### Fixes

- `method_get_block_media_query_declarations()` (`lib/blocks.php`) — added a default value (`''`) for the `$cssSelector` parameter to silence PHP warnings when it is called without one.
- `method_core_extensions_render_css()` (`method-core-extensions.php`) — guard against an empty/missing `blockName` before the config lookup, preventing a warning on blocks without a name.

## 2.0.0-beta14

### New Block — Fluid Video (`method/fluid-video`)

A click-to-play video embed block. The block renders a poster image with a play button; on click, the poster is swapped for an autoplaying YouTube or Vimeo iframe at a 16:9 aspect ratio.

- Supports YouTube (`youtube.com/watch`, `youtu.be/`, `embed`, `shorts`) and Vimeo (`vimeo.com/`, `player.vimeo.com/video/`, channel URLs) via the **Video URL** field.
- Color controls for link (play icon), link hover, background, and background shade — with custom labels in the inspector (e.g. "Icon Color", "Image Shade").
- Background image (poster) selection through `MethodBackgroundControls` in a limited mode that hides image-display, parallax, and video-fallback options.
- Border, border-radius, margin, and box-shadow controls per breakpoint.
- Frontend handler (`method-fluid-video.js`) builds the iframe on click, hides the poster, and moves focus into the player for keyboard users.

### Component Changes

- **`MethodColorControls`** — new `labels` prop accepts a `{ key: 'Custom Label' }` map to override the default label for any included color setting.
- **`MethodBackgroundControls`** — new `limited` prop that hides image-display options (shade, position, repeat, size, parallax checkbox, background video URL) for blocks that only need to pick a background image.
- **`MethodStyleTag.jsx`** — added `linkHoverColor` to the editor CSS generator so hover color previews live inside the block editor.

### Helpers

- New `method_parse_video_url( $url )` in `lib/helper-functions.php` returns `[ 'provider' => 'youtube'|'vimeo', 'id' => '...' ]` for supported URLs.
- New `method_build_embed_url( $provider, $id )` returns an autoplay-ready embed URL with sensible defaults (no related videos, modest branding, inline iOS playback, DNT for Vimeo).

### Build

- `gulpfile.js` — `assets/js/method-fluid-video.js` is now concatenated into `assets/js/scripts.js`.
- `lib/blocks.php` — registers the new `method-fluid-video` block.


